pires/articles/18-brumaire-the-context-and-course-of-a-coup-detat/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"65\",\"title\":\"Coup of 18 Brumaire - World History Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"May 18, 2023 · The coup brought Napoleon Bonaparte to power and, in the view of many historians, marked the end of the French Revolution (1789-1799).\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldhistory.org/Coup_of_18_Brumaire/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"66\",\"title\":\"Napoleon Rises to Power in France | Research Starters - EBSCO\",\"description\":\"Collaborating with influential figures like Emmanuel-Joseph Sieyès, Napoleon orchestrated a coup d'état on November 9, 1799 (18 Brumaire, Year VIII), ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/history/napoleon-rises-power-france\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"67\",\"title\":\"Coronation of Napoleon I - World History Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Jul 6, 2023 · The Coronation of Napoleon I as Emperor of the French took place on Sunday 2 December 1804, in the Notre-Dame de Paris cathedral.\",\"url\":\"https://www.worldhistory.org/article/2251/coronation-of-napoleon-i/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"68\",\"title\":\"Public services | Europeana\",\"description\":\"In 1800, Napoleon created the Bank of France to help the country to recover from a heavy economic and financial crisis. He introduced a currency of constant ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.europeana.eu/en/exhibitions/napoleon-and-urbanism-in-the-19th-century/public-services\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"69\",\"title\":\"Napoleon's Consecration and Coronation\",\"description\":\"On 18 May, 1804, after much political horse trading, the French Senate proclaimed Bonaparte Emperor Napoleon I.\",\"url\":\"https://www.napoleon.org/en/history-of-the-two-empires/articles/napoleons-consecration-and-coronation/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"70\",\"title\":\"Constitution of the Year XII - The Napoleon Series\",\"description\":\"The Emperor can fix the jointure of the Empress and assign it out of the civil list; his successors can change none of the dispositions which lie shall have ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.napoleon-series.org/research/government/legislation/c_constitution12.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"71\",\"title\":\"Major battles of all the campaigns constituting the Napoleonic Wars\",\"description\":\"While Marshal Davoust was victorious at Auerstaedt, the second part of the Prussian army was destroyed at Jena by Napoleon himself. The campaign had begun only ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.napoleon-empire.org/en/battles.php\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"72\",\"title\":\"8 Key Battles of Napoleon | TheCollector\",\"description\":\"Apr 30, 2025 · Jena and Auerstedt were fought on October 14, 1806, between Napoleon's forces and the Prussians at the beginning of the War of the Fourth ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.thecollector.com/key-battles-napoleon/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"73\",\"title\":\"Napoleon Bonaparte's Russian Campaign: The Patriotic War of 1812\",\"description\":\"The human cost of Napoleon Bonaparte's “Russian Campaign”—the Patriotic War of 1812—was staggering. Napoleon lost over 500,000 men, the core of his army.\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/napoleon-bonapartes-russian-campaign-the-patriotic-war-of-1812/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"74\",\"title\":\"Continental System, Napoleonic Wars, Blockade - France - Britannica\",\"description\":\"Napoleon launched the “Continental System”: in the Berlin Decree of November 1806, he prohibited British trade with all countries under French influence.\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/place/France/The-Continental-System\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"75\",\"title\":\"Napoleon abdicates the throne and is exiled to Elba | April 11, 1814\",\"description\":\"On April 11, 1814, Napoleon Bonaparte, emperor of France and one of the greatest military leaders in history, abdicates the throne.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/april-11/napoleon-exiled-to-elba\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"76\",\"title\":\"Battle of Waterloo | National Army Museum\",\"description\":\"Napoleon was defeated. He spoke of fighting on, but was forced to abdicate when the Allies entered Paris on 7 July. He spent the rest of his life in exile on ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.nam.ac.uk/explore/battle-waterloo\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"77\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://historyguild.org/france-after-1815/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"78\",\"title\":\"How France Overthrew Its King (Again) in the July Revolution of 1830\",\"description\":\"Jun 18, 2025 · In the last days of July 1830, a series of repressive ordinances issued by King Charles X provoked widespread protests. Led by liberals and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thecollector.com/july-revolution-1830-france-overthrew-king/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"79\",\"title\":\"Charles X and the July Revolution | History of Western Civilization II\",\"description\":\"In 1830 the discontent caused by Charles X's conservative policies and his nomination of the Ultra prince de Polignac as minister culminated in an uprising ...\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/suny-hccc-worldhistory2/chapter/charles-x-and-the-july-revolution/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"80\",\"title\":\"The July Monarchy (1830-1848) - Paris: Capital of the 19th Century\",\"description\":\"The July Monarchy saw the rise of the bourgeoisie, a return to Napoleonic influence, and a severe economic crisis. The February Revolution of 1848 ended the  ...Missing:  facts | Show results with:facts\",\"url\":\"https://library.brown.edu/cds/paris/chronology4.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"81\",\"title\":\"The July Monarchy | History of Western Civilization II - Lumen Learning\",\"description\":\"The July Monarchy was a liberal constitutional monarchy in France under Louis Philippe I, starting with the July Revolution of 1830.\",\"url\":\"https://co