d with the previous year, an increase of 1.5%.\",\"url\":\"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/statistics-explained/index.php?title=Crime_statistics\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"596\",\"title\":\"Europe: Crime Index by Country 2024 - Cost of Living\",\"description\":\"Europe: Crime Index by Country 2024. ; 1, France, 55.3 ; 2, Belarus, 50.8 ; 3, Belgium, 49.2 ; 4, Sweden, 48.4.Eastern Europe · Northern Europe · Southern Europe · Western Europe\",\"url\":\"https://www.numbeo.com/crime/rankings_by_country.jsp?title=2024\u0026region=150\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"597\",\"title\":\"Bataclan 6 Years On: The Attacks That Changed France\",\"description\":\"Nov 18, 2021 · November 13 marked the 6th anniversary of the Paris attacks - a series of simultaneous jihadist terrorist attacks that took place in 2015 ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.institutmontaigne.org/en/expressions/bataclan-6-years-attacks-changed-france\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"598\",\"title\":\"Country Reports on Terrorism 2023: France - State Department\",\"description\":\"Security services are concerned about “Islamist terrorism” and “ultra right ... Bureau of Counterterrorism Bureau of European and Eurasian Affairs ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.state.gov/reports/country-reports-on-terrorism-2023/france\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"599\",\"title\":\"Terrorism: France's International Action\",\"description\":\"International terrorism is one of the most serious threats to international peace and security. Since this threat has never been so strong, France is taking ...Missing:  2000-2025 | Show results with:2000-2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/en/french-foreign-policy/security-disarmament-and-non-proliferation/terrorism-france-s-international-action/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"600\",\"title\":\"Terrorism and violent extremism | Europol - European Union\",\"description\":\"The overall terrorist threat to the security of the EU remains acute. The main concern of Member States is jihadist terrorism and the closely related ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.europol.europa.eu/crime-areas/terrorism-and-violent-extremism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"601\",\"title\":\"Understanding Urban Riots in France - Brookings Institution\",\"description\":\"To get a better idea of the causes of the November 2005 urban riots in France, which have claimed 200 million euros in damaged property and one death, one ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.brookings.edu/articles/understanding-urban-riots-in-france/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"602\",\"title\":\"2005 French riots - Wikipedia\",\"description\":\"2005 French riots ; Deaths of Zyed Benna and Bouna Traoré [fr] · Arson, rioting · State of emergency declared on 8 November, rioting slows down by mid-November.Timeline · Context · Assessment of rioting · Response\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2005_French_riots\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"603\",\"title\":\"France riots: Why do the banlieues erupt time and time again? - BBC\",\"description\":\"Jul 3, 2023 · Marseille police officers arrested over riot death. Mohamed Bendriss may have died after being hit by a police weapon during the unrest earlier ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.com/news/world-europe-66071455\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"604\",\"title\":\"French Banlieues and the Consequences of Spatial Segregation\",\"description\":\"The 2005 banlieue rebellions were reactions to an attempt to control the behavior of the public through various social institutions, including the police force.\",\"url\":\"https://coascenters.howard.edu/french-banlieues-and-consequences-spatial-segregation\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"605\",\"title\":\"Opinion | These French Riots Are Different — and Far More Disturbing\",\"description\":\"Jul 7, 2023 · Those riots were sparked after two young men were chased to their death by police, and the conversation quickly focused on the fate of the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2023/07/07/french-riots-banlieues-00105143\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"606\",\"title\":\"ASSIMILATIONISM VS MULTICULTURALISM - Kenan Malik\",\"description\":\"Jan 12, 2015 · French 'assimilationist' policies are generally seen as the polar opposite of British-style multiculturalism.\",\"url\":\"https://kenanmalik.com/2015/01/12/assimilationism-vs-multiculturalism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"607\",\"title\":\"The Debate Over Multiculturalism: Philosophy, Politics, and Policy\",\"description\":\"Sep 22, 2011 · Most of the contemporary debate about multiculturalism centers on immigrants and their descendants rather than on longstanding minority groups.Missing:  preservation | Show results with:preservation\",\"url\":\"https://www.migrationpolicy.org/article/debate-over-multiculturalism-philosophy-politics-and-policy\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"608\",\"title\":\"Models of Integration in Europe - Fondation Robert Schuman\",\"description\":\"Oct 29, 2017 · The assimilation model, also known as \\\"the republican model\\\", claims blindness as far as cultural and religious differences are concerned.\",\"url\":\"https://www.robert-schuman.eu/en/european-issues/0449-models-of-integration-in-europe\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"609\",\"title\":\"French universalism sidelines ethnic minorities - The Conversation\",\"description\":\"May 9, 2023 · A multicultural republic should not despise universal rights. On the contrary, it should fight for all to have access to them.\",\"url\":\"https://theconversation.com/french-universalism-sidelines-ethnic-minorities-why-that-must-change-203609\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"610\",\"title\":\"Les Banlieues de France: how a failure of integration has led to the ...\",\"description\":\"Les Banlieues de France: how a failure of integration has led to the spread of extremism. December 5, 2018. World. By Samuel Driggers. More than 1,700 ...\",\"url\":\"https://georgiapoliticalreview.com/les-banlieues-de-france-how-a-failure-of-integration-has-led-to-the-spread-of-extremism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"611\",\"title\":\"Ethnicity, Islam, and les banlieues: Confusing the Issues - Items\",\"description\":\"The conflation of the otherwise discrete issues of the suburbs, immigration, and exclusion would become commonplace. The November 2005 riots did no more than ...\",\"url\":\"https://items.ssrc.org/riots-in-france/ethnicity-islam-and-les-banlieues-confusing-the-issues/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"612\",\"title\":\"The France Riots: Another Example of How Europe Is Committing ...\",\"description\":\"Jul 6, 2023 · ... ISSUES · CULTURE \u0026 SOCIETY. The France Riots: Another Example of How Europe Is Committing Suicide with Its Failed Immigration Policy. CULTURE ...Missing:  banlieues | Show results with:banlieues\",\"url\":\"https://www.hungarianconservative.com/articles/culture_society/france_riots_europe_failed_immigration_policy/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"613\",\"title\":\"Eric Zemmour, the anti-immigrant radical who could supplant Marine ...\",\"description\":\"Oct 12, 2021 · He says Islam has no place in France. Many voters seem to agree | Europe.Missing:  preservation | Show results with:preservation\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.economist.com/europe/eric-zemmour-the-anti-immigrant-radical-who-could-supplant-marine-le-pen/21805511\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"614\",\"title\":\"How France's far right changed the debate on immigration - France 24\",\"description\":\"Jun 20, 2024 · The far-right party's rise has fundamentally changed France's immigration debate, dragging besieged President Emmanuel Macron's once-liberal coalition far to ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.france24.com/en/france/20240620-how-france-s-far-right-changed-the-debate-on-immigration\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"615\",\"title\":\"Why does France reject multiculturalism? - Quora\",\"description\":\"Jun 30, 2019 · France, as a general rule of thumb, rejects multiculturalism. It doesn't mean that everyone must eat baguette and cheese every day, however it ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.quora.com/Why-does-France-reject-multiculturalism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"616\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.statista.com/statistics/960176/discussion-about-immigration-sensitive-topic-france/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"617\",\"title\":\"The French are becoming less nervous about migration, but ...\",\"description\":\"Jun 21, 2023 · While polls show demand for regulating immigration, they also find that the French are increasingly tolerant and more concerned about the cost of living and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.lemonde.fr/en/france/article/2023/06/21/the-french-are-becoming-less-nervous-about-migration-but-prejudices-persist_6034675_7.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"618\",\"title\":\"Stagnation in the French Banlieues - Global Challenges\",\"description\":\"Over the years, French urban renewal policies have failed to fix deep-rooted issues in the banlieues, relying on superficial solutions while social ...Missing:  failures | Show results with:failures\",\"url\":\"https://globalchallenges.ch/issue/special_2/stagnation-in-the-french-banlieues/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"619\",\"title\":\"Commentary: French assimilation vs. British multiculturalism - Euractiv\",\"description\":\"Nov 15, 2005 · The right balance between the French integration model of assimilation and the British model of multiculturalism needs to be struck, he argues.\",\"url\":\"https://www.euractiv.com/opinion/commentary-french-assimilation-vs-british-multiculturalism-what-integration-model-for-europe/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"620\",\"title\":\"3 Things to Know About France's Immigration Law Backlash\",\"description\":\"Jan 25, 2024 · French public opinion on immigration more broadly, however, is nuanced. Some reports and studies indicate that French people have actually ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.usnews.com/news/best-countries/articles/2024-01-24/3-things-to-know-about-france